{
  "about": "How a text file's bytes are decoded (docs/dev/documents.md 'Text extraction'): gamma/documents/text.py decode and frontend/src/documents/viewers/textLoad.js decodeText of a whole file. A byte-order mark picks UTF-8, UTF-16LE or UTF-16BE and is no text; anything else is UTF-8 with each bad sequence a U+FFFD (bad true); no code-page guess. binary: a NUL anywhere in the decoded text, or U+FFFD more than BAD_SHARE (5%) of its characters; text is then '' and bad false. The line breaks are as written (\\r\\n is folded by the readers after, not here). bytes is base64. encoding is the backend's codec name (utf-8, utf-8-sig, utf-16-le, utf-16-be); the client has no such output (its byteOrderMark names utf-8 with skip 3, utf-16le and utf-16be), so the node half compares text, bad and binary only. Read by backend/tests/test_shared_fixtures.py and frontend/tests/textLoad.test.mjs.",
